## review(#238): dedupe materialise filter, reject empty objects, retarget to 0.9.4

Context: Review follow-ups on PR #238 (fix for #236 - rule triples with literal
objects dropped at materialisation). The PR was rebased onto the `0.9.4` branch
and its changelog moved from `v0.9.3` to `v0.9.4` (current pyproject version).

Changes:
1. src/back/objects/digitaltwin/build/TwinInferredMaterialize.py - `uri_triples`
   is now the single materialise filter: URI subject + URI predicate, literal or
   URI object, but the object must be non-empty (empty/whitespace/missing objects
   are dropped). Added a docstring explaining the rule.
2. src/back/objects/digitaltwin/TwinBackgroundTasks.py - `run_inference_task` now
   delegates to new `TwinInferredMaterialize.from_inferred` (wraps `uri_triples`) instead of re-implementing
   the same predicate (removes duplication; the two sites can no longer drift).
3. tests/units/dtwin/test_v090_twin_build_prepare.py - parametrised test that
   empty / whitespace / missing objects, the `(batch)` placeholder subject and a
   non-URI predicate are dropped.
4. tests/units/dtwin/test_v090_twin_background_tasks.py - test that the scheduled
   / API inference materialise path drops `(batch)` and empty-object triples while
   keeping literal ones.
5. changelogs/v0.9.4/AlexPicard10_2026-11-24.log - moved from v0.9.3 (version
   alignment).

Modified files:
- src/back/objects/digitaltwin/TwinBackgroundTasks.py
- src/back/objects/digitaltwin/build/TwinInferredMaterialize.py
- tests/units/dtwin/test_v090_twin_build_prepare.py
- tests/units/dtwin/test_v090_twin_background_tasks.py
- changelogs/v0.9.4/AlexPicard10_2026-11-24.log (moved)

Tests: `uv run --frozen pytest -q -m "not scenario"` -> 9717 passed, 338 skipped, 8 deselected.
(The size-budget architecture test required extracting `TwinInferredMaterialize.from_inferred`
so `run_inference_task` does not grow past its baseline.)

## review(#239): exact transitive-chain rule, UI property-chain export, retarget to 0.9.4

Context: Review follow-ups on PR #239 (axiom-driven graph reasoning, #237). The PR
was retargeted from `master` to `0.9.4`; its changelog was merged into the
existing `v0.9.4` AlexPicard10 file.

Changes:
1. src/back/core/reasoning/ReasoningService.py - `_find_transitive_from_axioms`
   now requires a chain of exactly two elements (`p ∘ p ⊑ p`). Longer self-chains
   (`p ∘ p ∘ p ⊑ p`) do not imply transitivity and are ignored.
2. src/back/core/w3c/owl/OntologyGenerator.py - `propertyChain` axioms now fall
   back to `subject` when `resultProperty` is absent (the Add-Axiom UI stores the
   result property as `subject`; the parser emits `resultProperty`), so UI-created
   chains are really exported to OWL. A `null` chain no longer raises `TypeError`.
   Size-neutral to respect the architecture size ratchet.
3. src/front/static/ontology/js/ontology-axioms.js - the subject label reads
   "Result Property" for `propertyChain`.
4. tests/units/ontology/test_reasoning_service.py - 3-element self-chain negative
   case, imported (`resultProperty`) shape, missing-key / null-chain cases.
5. tests/units/ontology/test_owl_generator.py - UI `subject` shape is exported as
   `owl:propertyChainAxiom`; a null chain is skipped.
6. changelogs/v0.9.4/AlexPicard10_2026-11-24.log - PR #239 section merged here
   (removed from `v0.9.3`).

Modified files:
- src/back/core/reasoning/ReasoningService.py
- src/back/core/w3c/owl/OntologyGenerator.py
- src/front/static/ontology/js/ontology-axioms.js
- tests/units/ontology/test_reasoning_service.py
- tests/units/ontology/test_owl_generator.py
